	<title>We</title>
	<isbn>0140185852</isbn>
	<publication_year>1993</publication_year>
	<language_code>eng</language_code>
	<description>&lt;i&gt;WE&lt;/i&gt; tells the story of the minutely organized United State, where all citizens are not individuals but only he-Numbers and she-Numbers existing in identical glass apartments with every action regulated by the "Table of Hours." It is a community dedicated to the proposition that freedom and happiness are incompatible; that most men believe their freedom to be more than a fair exchange for a high level of materialistic happiness.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;i&gt;WE&lt;/i&gt; is recognized as the inspiration for George Orwell's famous &lt;i&gt;1984&lt;/i&gt;, and wasn't published in Russia until 1988 due to official censorship. It is generally regarded as a classic Utopian novel and an historic landmark in Soviet literature.</description>
